    Microsoft has not reviewed, endorsed or supported them. They are:

    1. docker/Dockerfile, .github/workflows/pull-request.yml
       Removed the unpinned "npm install -g npm", which pulled an npm requiring
       Node 22+ into an image pinned to Node 18 and broke the build; copied
       jest.config.json so the image can run its own tests; added a Docker
       build step to pull-request CI.

    2. src/check-token.ts, src/__tests__/check-token.test.ts
       Read the standard Authorization header rather than the non-standard
       Authentication header, so REQUIRE_AUTH=true no longer rejects every
       correct client. Added the middleware's first tests.

    3. src/check-token.ts, src/__tests__/check-token.test.ts
       Stopped an unresolvable signing key from terminating the process;
       return 500 rather than 403 when the check cannot be performed; cache
       signing keys.

    4. src/index.ts, src/client/index.js, src/utility-apis.ts
       Made the landing page default a relative path, so it is correct at any
       published host port.

    5. src/subscription-api-impl.ts, src/__tests__/subscription-api-activate-term.test.ts
       Fixed the subscription term start date, which was set one term in the
       future.

    6. src/helpers/queue-helper.ts, src/__tests__/queue-helper-renew.test.ts
       Made Renew advance the subscription term instead of silently doing
       nothing. The behaviour is inferred, not documented by Microsoft.

    Plus corrections to README.md, SUPPORT.md, SECURITY.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,
    docs/*.md, rest_calls/*.http and a source comment, as recorded in the
    repository history.

